{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.542918Z","id":"32f2a2bb176b311efceeb273587a72804117cc77007d5876c5663683cdee03f4","body":{"detail":"_cancel pops the screen and drops the attempt's result, but the Future from Launcher.make keeps running, so the agent still calls createArtifact and the app appears in the launcher (lib/ui/launcher.dart _onEvent) after the person cancelled. The make signature in the plan (Future<String> Function(String request)) carries no cancel signal, and AgentLoop.newApp(String) (plan Task F4b) takes none either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":98},"content_hash":"7ca33a2900a53644f52b5ff4b0a9d74da288bfdc558a7833cd30a0aaf16c1e1c"},"suggested_fix":"Give make a cancel signal (for example a Future<void> the screen completes on Cancel) and pass it to the backend as AgentRequest.cancelled, so a cancelled run creates nothing.","summary":"Cancel on the making screen abandons the run but does not stop it: the new app still lands","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.543019Z","id":"fdb9b26782663b9fa19f2d5b0be6ff925455111c36edbbbb91062a8eba1524ee","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 6.1 starts the say-usable timer on submit and stops it on the new app's first ready. Launcher has no Timings, so the make callback is the only place that sees the submit. Whoever builds Launcher (AppRoot, plan Task F9) must call timings.start(sayUsable) inside make before AgentLoop.newApp, or no say-usable record is ever written.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"5bd238290e24231180b1f26a2e922e0187c1ad6e815a0027c834fc1cf8bc3e69"},"summary":"Submit does not start the say-usable timer here; the make passed in has to","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.543053Z","id":"782d52488d2d36a10c5e4249160db6eb9fa7369c5b7ff7a27c0347579f2b84cb","body":{"detail":"The tile list is listArtifacts once at start plus version and artifact_deleted events. Stream errors are ignored, and nothing reloads after a daemon restart, where events missed while the daemon was down (or IDs a new daemon does not resume from Last-Event-ID) leave the grid stale until a pull to refresh.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"eeb475356a5701b9b777821c904ef2c55a2f9496e769d48a18dc6d3d9a843c24"},"suggested_fix":"Reload with listArtifacts when the event stream reconnects or the daemon endpoint changes (AppRoot knows both).","summary":"The launcher never reloads its list after the event stream drops events","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.972098Z","id":"5d09634475a2480647d4de7478890b5a505a18d9ab03720a5d446bcac7c223ad","body":{"detail":"Failure: tap New app, submit any request, tap Cancel (or system back) while 'Making' shows; AgentLoop.newApp keeps running, calls createArtifact, and the launcher's version event adds the tile the person cancelled. Launcher.make (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart:30) is Future<String> Function(String) and carries no cancel signal, although AgentLoop.newApp(request, {Future<void>? cancelled}) (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:114) and AgentRequest.cancelled now exist. _cancel (making_screen.dart:95) and the PopScope (making_screen.dart:110) only bump _attempt. No test covers cancel stopping the run.","kind":"blocker","references":"32f2a2bb176b311efceeb273587a72804117cc77007d5876c5663683cdee03f4","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":98},"content_hash":"7ca33a2900a53644f52b5ff4b0a9d74da288bfdc558a7833cd30a0aaf16c1e1c"},"suggested_fix":"Change make to Future<String> Function(String request, Future<void> cancelled); MakingScreen owns a Completer<void> per attempt, completes it on Cancel, back, Open Settings, Edit, dispose and Retry-of-a-stale-attempt, and treats AgentError.cancelled as a silent end. Widget test: Cancel completes the future make received, and a make that honours it never calls open.","summary":"Cancel and back on the making screen do not stop the run: the cancelled app is still created and appears in the launcher","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.972568Z","id":"7a14c0c260ca5cda20193669a49725b134abd00d7faefe8dd92c329c272acf67","body":{"detail":"Failure: open the launcher, let the daemon restart (app resume after Android kills it, or a new daemon epoch) and create or delete an artifact in the gap; ClaxApi.events (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart:102-107) delivers ready{resumed:false} or resync, which _onEvent drops because they carry no artifact_id, so the new app is missing (or the deleted one still shown) until a manual pull to refresh. The initial ready is also ignored, so a version event that lands between listArtifacts and the stream opening can be lost. No test pushes ready/resync.","kind":"blocker","references":"782d52488d2d36a10c5e4249160db6eb9fa7369c5b7ff7a27c0347579f2b84cb","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"37e3197b5ffc01331c4c3414fe9feda8fac1a55f0e0fc1137bcf2c83730bd9bf"},"suggested_fix":"In _onEvent, call _load() on resync and on ready whose data.resumed is not true; test with FakeClaxApi that a resync after an out-of-band seedArtifact shows the new tile.","summary":"The launcher ignores the event stream's ready{resumed:false} and resync, so its grid stays stale after a daemon restart","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/new_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.972902Z","id":"5ef533b41b5df2b991505e8efb31f6e518890159e0ba2bf9d282cb39f1ee158b","body":{"detail":"VoiceDenied/VoiceUnsupported disable the mic and put the reason in the Tooltip (new_sheet.dart:202); status (line 147) shows only a voice error or 'Listening…', so on touch the person sees a greyed mic-off icon with no explanation unless they long-press it. The launcher's FAB carries a mic icon (launcher.dart:133), so the promise of voice silently fails. Android stops re-prompting after a second refusal, so retrying availability() is not enough; rendered at 412x892 the denied sheet shows no text at all about why.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"f89c8438ceb8b8ce9392fb966d5cfdc1ffa7b8451332804e7ace010cacf99e73"},"suggested_fix":"Show micReason in the status line when the mic is unavailable, and for VoiceDenied offer an action that opens the app's system settings (e.g. the permission_handler or app_settings plugin's openAppSettings).","summary":"With the mic denied the reason is only a tooltip, invisible on a phone, and nothing leads to the permission setting","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.973028Z","id":"4fd5aa1d184a730e40041249421322c6dc6c7226f7d3cbacacba23c3e48ff437","body":{"detail":"On a fresh phone install the backend is the Messages API with no key. The person taps New app, dictates, taps Make it, and only then sees 'Add your Claude API key in Settings' (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:106) on the failure screen. Launcher has no way to know a key is missing.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"b80eb65d6027f3d4b3d2ef812b226a35d4b4fb6bdb84bf3610e02a6f5529f920"},"suggested_fix":"Give Launcher an optional 'needsSetup' message (AppRoot computes it from SecureKey and the backend) and show a banner or the empty state 'Add your Claude API key to start' with an Open Settings button.","summary":"With no API key the first New app runs to a failure; the launcher could say so before the person speaks","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.973179Z","id":"c6bfa8ec9de151dd6ce2207f53528e0caf71d9acebdf56768aee8b0ba2f8e512","body":{"detail":"On a phone the field reads 'Claude API key' with helper 'Kept in this device's secure storage'; nothing says the key is created at console.anthropic.com (Settings, API keys) or that it starts with sk-ant-, and there is no paste button, which is the realistic way to enter it on a phone.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"7bc79cfcdabb4ea0d93c625a92aca9b36ca4fc798787959b40ebadec5d87ce46"},"suggested_fix":"Helper text 'Create one at console.anthropic.com, then paste it here', a paste suffix action reading Clipboard, and a light format check (sk-ant- prefix) before Save key.","summary":"The key field does not say where a key comes from","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.973291Z","id":"44f41716054407ea3700b8ffc53bd1b6dee1ccfe4f8fc58a90fece0318ca08bb","body":{"detail":"Rendered at phone size it shows the sparkle icon, 'Making “a run tracker with weekly”…', an indeterminate bar and '7 s'. Generation takes tens of seconds; nothing says what is happening (writing, checking, publishing) or what is typical, and the five-word cut ends mid-phrase.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"a1f0e5ae0c8da6b83ff7fbbb7835326ecce852a028b2c61cc3baed440e898839"},"suggested_fix":"Let make report phases (the loop knows: prompt sent, result validated, resend after a validation failure, publishing) through an optional ValueListenable<String> and show it under the bar; after ~20 s add 'Usually under a minute'.","summary":"The making screen is an indeterminate bar and a seconds count; it has no sense of stage","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
